17 {"Field": "Account", "Value": "Mac-Gray, the second-largest US laundry facilities management contractor, had BofA Merrill Lynch sound out strategic rival Party A in April 2013; Party A made an unsolicited $17.00-$19.00 proposal on June 21. On June 24 a new Special Committee decided to consider a sale, and BofA contacted 50 parties (15 strategic, 35 financial), 20 of which signed confidentiality agreements. Preliminary indications from CSC/Pamplona ($18.50), Party B ($17.00-$18.00) and Party C ($15.00-$17.00, then $16.00-$16.50) led the committee to advance four bidders, including Party A, to management meetings and staged data-room access, with less customer data shown to strategic bidders. Revised indications on September 9-10 ranged from $16.00 to $19.50. A request for final indications by September 18 drew $20.75 from CSC/Pamplona, a $21.50 cash-plus-options package from Party B, Party A's unchanged $18.00-$19.00 and nothing from Party C. The committee preferred CSC/Pamplona's fully Pamplona-funded offer for its certainty, asked for $21.25, and signed exclusivity on September 24 once CSC/Pamplona agreed. After one extension of exclusivity, the merger agreement was signed on October 14, 2013 at $21.25 per share in cash and announced on October 15."}

